  "description": "A modest single-storey ground-floor extension to the rear/side;\n\nRefinement of the ground-floor extension roof to complete a coherent sloping roof form, with a small rear/side flat or mansard-style section incorporating a discreet rooflight;\n\nFuture Replacement of existing windows with traditional timber casement windows;\n\nFuture Replacement of the front door with a traditional nine-panel timber door;\n\nReplacement of an existing shed with a modest garden room within the rear courtyard;\n\nMinor boundary and landscaping works to the front and rear gardens.\n\nProvision of a roof window in the existing East facing roof towards the Green.The roof window is modest in size, aligned with existing roof geometry, and located discreetly so as not to interrupt the uniform roofscape when viewed from the Green. A flush, heritage style window is proposed.\n\nNo additional storeys, roof extensions, or changes to the principal roof form are proposed.\n\nAll proposed works are limited to areas of low visibility and avoid alteration to principal elevations or the established roof form.",
